  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Old 2.0 avatars with the multiple animators inventory system are now broken. This system is very widely used, and a large number of 2.0 avatars are now broken.\nFor reference, the inventory system works by having multiple animators that effect the avatar in different ways, most usually turning on or off gameobjects. These animators are set to off by default, so their animations do not play immediately. The avatar's main animator can turn these animators on in either emote or gesture animations using the \"Behavior\" keyframe (which turns on/off the first component of a gameobject). Once the emote/gesture stops playing the animator is set to off again, and this freezes the animation in its current state. So if the animator turned on a gameobject, then it will stay on until another animator turns it off.\nWhat appears to be happening now is that on loading an avatar, all the animators on an avatar are briefly turned on even if they were off by default. This causes every inventory toggle to go off at once. Unity executes animations in order that their animators appear in the hierarcy. If the animator to set the avatar back to its default state is last in the hierarchy, everything will be fine. However, in most cases this isn't true and avatar will have a bunch of stuff toggled on/off that shouldn't be. Also, the toggling of everything on at once could potentially break some inventory systems entirely.",
